refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public Time\DurationTime\Duration::divideBy intdivisor
Returns a duration that is this duration divided by divisor. Any remaining fraction of a nanosecond is truncated, so the result is rounded towards zero. The sign of the duration is preserved.

&reftitle.parameters;
divisor
The divisor. Must be greater than 0.

&reftitle.errors;
If divisor is negative, a ValueError is thrown.
If divisor is 0, a DivisionByZeroError is thrown.

  &reftitle.examples;

   Time\Duration::divideBy example


<?php
// Fractions of a nanosecond are truncated.
var_dump(\Time\Duration::fromSeconds(10)->divideBy(3)->multiplyBy(3));

try {
    \Time\Duration::fromSeconds(10)->divideBy(0);
} catch (DivisionByZeroError $e) {
    echo $e->getMessage(), PHP_EOL;
}


